(5) be prepared at a reasonable scale;

(6) specify where on-site or off-site quantitative and qualitative controls are to be implemented;

(7) be consistent with the General Performance Standards for Stormwater Management in Maryland, found in Section 1.2 of the State’s Design Manual; and

(8) be approved by the State Water Management Administration.

